SPAdes 4.2.0 -> Emscripten: meaningful memory figure in the log.

emscripten's getrusage() stub fills only ru_utime/ru_stime, so get_max_rss() returned
uninitialised stack memory and every log line showed a random memory column (e.g.
"1511828488193G"). Report the WebAssembly heap size (which only grows, i.e. the peak) instead.
get_max_rss() is used only for logging and for SPAdes' free-memory estimate, which is
"unlimited minus used" here as on native macOS (setrlimit fails on both), so outputs are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/common/utils/memory_limit.cpp b/src/common/utils/memory_limit.cpp
index b5e3ca0..cd0e175 100644
--- a/src/common/utils/memory_limit.cpp
+++ b/src/common/utils/memory_limit.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 
 #include <sys/time.h>
 #include <sys/resource.h>
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+# include <emscripten/heap.h>
+#endif
 
 #include "config.hpp"
 
@@ -77,6 +80,12 @@ size_t get_max_rss() {
 
   return t_info.resident_size / 1024;
 }
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+// emscripten's getrusage() leaves ru_maxrss unset (garbage in every log line); report the
+// WebAssembly heap size instead (it only grows, so it is the peak), in KiB like ru_maxrss.
+size_t get_max_rss() {
+    return emscripten_get_heap_size() / 1024;
+}
 #else
 
 size_t get_max_rss() {
